          <p>The three families concatenate into a <strong>97-dimensional vector</strong>, regressed with random forest, gradient boosting, XGBoost, stacking, and stepwise models. Capturing only low-order statistics, they are outperformed by frozen DINOv2 descriptors by <strong>30.7%</strong> (Balakot) and <strong>33.1%</strong> (Karlsruhe) relative error.</p>
