    <h1>Conclusions &amp; Future Work</h1>
    <div class="slide-body">
      <div class="col">
        <ul class="points">
          <li><strong>Self-supervised features suffice.</strong> A frozen, ImageNet-pretrained DINOv2 encodes enough canopy structure for accurate RGB-only AGB, with no multispectral, LiDAR, or fine-tuning.</li>
          <li><strong>Selection is essential.</strong> The full 384-D vector consistently underperforms a correlation-ranked subset for all regressors at small n.</li>
          <li><strong>Clustering helps heterogeneity.</strong> Cluster-specific models lift accuracy, most for tree models, and degrade gracefully to a single model otherwise.</li>
          <li><strong>Operational reach.</strong> High-resolution carbon mapping is feasible from standard aerial RGB and a public vision model, lowering the cost barrier for data-sparse regions like Pakistan.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
